How can I use Java to scrape news articles about the US political situation and save the headlines, authors, and publish dates in a CSV file? What are some ways I can handle potential errors or exceptions during the scraping process?
Here's a sample Java code using the Jsoup library to scrape news articles from a website:
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;
import org.jsoup.select.Elements;
import java.io.File;
import java.io.FileWriter;
import java.io.IOException;
public class NewsScraper {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            // Connect to the website and get the HTML
            Document document = Jsoup.connect("https://www.newswebsite.com/politics/us").get();
            // Get the headlines, authors, and publish dates
            Elements headlines = document.select("h2.article-headline");
            Elements authors = document.select("span.article-author");
            Elements dates = document.select("span.article-date");
            // Create a CSV file and write the data
            File file = new File("news_articles.csv");
            FileWriter writer = new FileWriter(file);
            writer.write("Headline,Author,Publish Date\n");
            for (int i = 0; i < headlines.size(); i++) {
                String headline = headlines.get(i).text();
                String author = authors.get(i).text();
                String date = dates.get(i).text();
                writer.write(headline + "," + author + "," + date + "\n");
            }
            writer.close();
            System.out.println("Successfully scraped and saved news articles!");
        } catch (IOException e) {
            // Handle any IO exceptions that may occur
            e.printStackTrace();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Handle any other exceptions that may occur
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
To handle potential errors or exceptions, I used a try-catch block to catch IO exceptions that may occur when connecting to the website or writing to the CSV file. I also added a catch block for any other exceptions that may occur during the scraping process.

